{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 400}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 104, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 3 leaves only edge 4 feeding the output, risking near-disconnection and large accuracy collapse (e.g., #229, #209, #303)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 3 is already none, deleting edge 5 removes a main path to the output and can disconnect the cell (e.g., #258, #357)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-to-output edge, all information must flow through node 1, so removing edge 0 is far more damaging (e.g., #56, #263)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, edge 1 may be the only route from input into intermediate nodes, so removing it is catastrophic (e.g., #316, #369)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free avg pool on the first edge with a 3x3 conv adds much more capacity than replacing an existing conv (e.g., #17, #231, #343 vs #134, #294)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the direct conv3x3 path to the output for pooling removes key learned capacity, hurting much more than replacing a skip (e.g., #3, #66, #352 vs #211, #381)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading the final edge from pooling to a 3x3 conv yields large gains, while replacing an existing conv gives little (e.g., #323, #366 vs #348)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "R